Falsifies `usb::verification::the_configuration_walk_is_total_and_accepts_only_an_interrupt_in`.

The defect: the endpoint filter stops checking the direction bit, so an interrupt OUT endpoint (the LED
endpoint some keyboards carry) is returned as the keyboard's input endpoint.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(k.endpoint & 0x80 != 0, "an IN endpoint")`.

